<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50456" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ventĭto</span></b> , āre,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq.
			n.</i> [id.], <i>to come often</i>, <i>be wont to come</i>, <i>keep coming</i>, <i>resort</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">multum ad eos (Ubios) mercatores ventitant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes. B.
					G. 4, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum ipse ad Scaevolam ventitarem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Leg. 1, 4, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Rep. 1, 9, 14</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 5, 27</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in castra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 11, 27, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum ventitabas, quo puella ducebat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat. 8,
					4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad potum (elephanti),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 52 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			</div>
